Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Spruce-Needles Choke the Dynamo
- Story & Context: When a November blizzard shattered the glass of the Andenes lighthouse generator shed, keeper Torstein Lind dragged three storm-fallen spruce saplings inside to shield the diesel dynamo, filling the freezing air with the sharp, resinous tang of crushed sap and hot copper. Trapped by forty-knot gales, Torstein spliced his field microphone into the station’s distress transmitter and began cycling guttural, overtone-rich didgeridoo drones against a sparse three-note jazz piano pattern to keep approaching coal freighters off the shoals. Over the hiss of maritime channel 16, his cracked falsetto sang the hook: "the root will split the copper before the dawn finds us." The transmission was logged by four passing vessels whose logbooks described the broadcast as a living, breathing foghorn made of marrow and spruce.
